{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '130,230p' ../agent-source/config.go; grep -R -n -i 'same.*timeout\\\\|timeout.*same\\\\|identical.*config\\\\|lease' ../agent-source/README.md ../agent-source/docs ../agent-source/membership.md ../agent-source/config.go; cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../product-schemas.json'))['DirectCheckPlan']\nprint('PLAN',json.dumps({k:v for k,v in s.items() if k\"'!='\"'\"'$defs'\"'},indent=2))\nprint('DEFS',list(s['\"'$defs'\"']))\nt=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']\nfor k in ['CheckSubmission','ClaimDraft','BindingDraft']:\n print(k,json.dumps(t[k],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"const (\n\t// SnapshotVersionMin is the minimum snapshot version\n\tSnapshotVersionMin SnapshotVersion = 0\n\t// SnapshotVersionMax is the maximum snapshot version\n\tSnapshotVersionMax = 1\n)\n\n// Config provides any necessary configuration for the Raft server.\ntype Config struct {\n\t// ProtocolVersion allows a Raft server to inter-operate with older\n\t// Raft servers running an older version of the code. This is used to\n\t// version the wire protocol as well as Raft-specific log entries that\n\t// the server uses when _speaking_ to other servers. There is currently\n\t// no auto-negotiation of versions so all servers must be manually\n\t// configured with compatible versions. See ProtocolVersionMin and\n\t// ProtocolVersionMax for the versions of the protocol that this server\n\t// can _understand_.\n\tProtocolVersion ProtocolVersion\n\n\t// HeartbeatTimeout specifies the time in follower state without contact\n\t// from a leader before we attempt an election.\n\tHeartbeatTimeout time.Duration\n\n\t// ElectionTimeout specifies the time in candidate state without contact\n\t// from a leader before we attempt an election.\n\tElectionTimeout time.Duration\n\n\t// CommitTimeout specifies the time without an Apply operation before the\n\t// leader sends an AppendEntry RPC to followers, to ensure a timely commit of\n\t// log entries.\n\t// Due to random staggering, may be delayed as much as 2x this value.\n\tCommitTimeout time.Duration\n\n\t// MaxAppendEntries controls the maximum number of append entries\n\t// to send at once. We want to strike a balance between efficiency\n\t// and avoiding waste if the follower is going to reject because of\n\t// an inconsistent log.\n\tMaxAppendEntries int\n\n\t// BatchApplyCh indicates whether we should buffer applyCh\n\t// to size MaxAppendEntries. This enables batch log commitment,\n\t// but breaks the timeout guarantee on Apply. Specifically,\n\t// a log can be added to the applyCh buffer but not actually be\n\t// processed until after the specified timeout.\n\tBatchApplyCh bool\n\n\t// If we are a member of a cluster, and RemovePeer is invoked for the\n\t// local node, then we forget all peers and transition into the follower state.\n\t// If ShutdownOnRemove is set, we additional shutdown Raft. Otherwise,\n\t// we can become a leader of a cluster containing only this node.\n\tShutdownOnRemove bool\n\n\t// TrailingLogs controls how many logs we leave after a snapshot. This is used\n\t// so that we can quickly replay logs on a follower instead of being forced to\n\t// send an entire snapshot. The value passed here is the initial setting used.\n\t// This can be tuned during operation using ReloadConfig.\n\tTrailingLogs uint64\n\n\t// SnapshotInterval controls how often we check if we should perform a\n\t// snapshot. We randomly stagger between this value and 2x this value to avoid\n\t// the entire cluster from performing a snapshot at once. The value passed\n\t// here is the initial setting used. This can be tuned during operation using\n\t// ReloadConfig.\n\tSnapshotInterval time.Duration\n\n\t// SnapshotThreshold controls how many outstanding logs there must be before\n\t// we perform a snapshot. This is to prevent excessive snapshotting by\n\t// replaying a small set of logs instead. The value passed here is the initial\n\t// setting used. This can be tuned during operation using ReloadConfig.\n\tSnapshotThreshold uint64\n\n\t// LeaderLeaseTimeout is used to control how long the \"lease\" lasts\n\t// for being the leader without being able to contact a quorum\n\t// of nodes. If we reach this interval without contact, we will\n\t// step down as leader.\n\tLeaderLeaseTimeout time.Duration\n\n\t// LocalID is a unique ID for this server across all time. When running with\n\t// ProtocolVersion < 3, you must set this to be the same as the network\n\t// address of your transport.\n\tLocalID ServerID\n\n\t// NotifyCh is used to provide a channel that will be notified of leadership\n\t// changes. Raft will block writing to this channel, so it should either be\n\t// buffered or aggressively consumed.\n\tNotifyCh chan<- bool\n\n\t// LogOutput is used as a sink for logs, unless Logger is specified.\n\t// Defaults to os.Stderr.\n\tLogOutput io.Writer\n\n\t// LogLevel represents a log level. If the value does not match a known\n\t// logging level hclog.NoLevel is used.\n\tLogLevel string\n\n\t// Logger is a user-provided logger. If nil, a logger writing to\n\t// LogOutput with LogLevel is used.\n\tLogger hclog.Logger\n\n\t// NoSnapshotRestoreOnStart controls if raft will restore a snapshot to the\n\t// FSM on start. This is useful if your FSM recovers from other mechanisms\n../agent-source/README.md:17:Please check your installation with:\n../agent-source/README.md:41:## Tagged Releases\n../agent-source/README.md:63:A high level overview of the Raft protocol is described below, but for details please read the full\n../agent-source/docs/README.md:95:      * checkLease (periodically LeaseTimeout) -\n../agent-source/config.go:201:\t// LeaderLeaseTimeout is used to control how long the \"lease\" lasts\n../agent-source/config.go:205:\tLeaderLeaseTimeout time.Duration\n../agent-source/config.go:327:\t\tLeaderLeaseTimeout: 500 * time.Millisecond,\n../agent-source/config.go:366:\tif config.LeaderLeaseTimeout < 5*time.Millisecond {\n../agent-source/config.go:367:\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"LeaderLeaseTimeout is too low\")\n../agent-source/config.go:369:\tif config.LeaderLeaseTimeout > config.HeartbeatTimeout {\n../agent-source/config.go:370:\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"LeaderLeaseTimeout (%s) cannot be larger than heartbeat timeout (%s)\", config.LeaderLeaseTimeout, config.HeartbeatTimeout)\nEXECUTION Observe actual implementation effects under explicit inputs, caller policy and authorized isolation. Contract applicability may remain unresolved during exploration; execution permission may not. A changed value or tests_passed is not a violation oracle. Exploration remains construction knowledge: a later requirement needs a separately fixed check, fresh execution and correspondence review, not retroactive relabelling. Missing capability, compilation failure, timeout, panic and a completed property comparison remain distinct. Retain failures; never precompute expected observations or alter protocol behavior to create a finding.\n\nCOMPLETION Initialization, driver compliance and observation validity belong in prerequisites, controls or diagnostics, not duplicate properties. Check a wait's return or record actual attainment when it establishes a necessary premise; when waiting is the investigated behavior, requiring success would discard the failure history. Sleep establishes elapsed time, not synchronization, completion or a coherent snapshot; a printed readiness flag is not a prerequisite witness. A diagnostic control need not satisfy the principal scenario's premises or acquire a separate obligation: select formal applicability from independently declared input/policy fields before execution, retaining control output. Distinct formal scenarios need their actual admission and premises; incompatible histories may need separate checks. Never select scenarios by observed results or missing premises after execution. Role readiness does not imply that earlier work drained. Across preparation, policy changes and delivery, preserve caller/transport duties; prefer one policy-selected delivery path and record the identity, provenance and order needed for attribution. Distinguish receipt, per-message-type queueing and dispatch; preserve the replaced layer's ordering without assuming global FIFO or arbitrary reordering. Legal in-flight work need not be emptied. End controlled work independently of the forbidden behavior. Observe admission, completion and final state for the same operation before treating absence as bounded holds. Missing completion, identity, result events and tool timeout remain unknown. A finite window records non-completion, not a deadline violation or infinite stalling. A repeatable suffix must account for behavior-determining state, schedule, queues, timers and callbacks; equal business fields do not close execution. A rescue stimulus may itself be required caller work.\n\nCORRELATION Monitor.admission_alias explicitly selects the declared harness prerequisite admitting operations whose completion is owed. It is not the first prerequisite by array order. Harness.prerequisites contains prerequisite events only; monitors select independent result events. ObservableProperty.identity_fields declares the stable operation identity once, using fields present at the relevant observation points. Do not repeat a result as a prerequisite or duplicate each identity equality as a Comparison. Reference conditions declare necessary predecessor relationships; unrelated prerequisites have no implicit list order. Assertions may refer to any declared prerequisite alias that actually precedes the result. Missing identity/reference fields or nonunique associations remain unknown. Independent applicability is checked before requiring unrelated history. Alias-dependent applicability follows correlation. Each operation is matched separately. A complete violating witness survives missing results in demonstrably independent operations, while coverage remains partial. Same-witness ambiguity and potentially global parse loss still block attribution. Use independent identity, not the compared value, to associate an input and output. A context expected to change cannot also be an equality filter. More complex histories need actual correlated prerequisites and results; unsupported general temporal expressions remain a stated limitation.\n\nMEANING Distinguish the written obligation, the proposition encoded by applicability/trigger/antecedent/assertion, and what this execution actually compared. Type, count or numeric-position equality may be necessary without establishing content or identity equality. Record comparisons and scope limits separately. Identify live object, copy, cache or caller-maintained observations, their writers and the synchronization or ownership boundary supporting the read; multiple fields must represent the state the proposition needs. Include ownership of injection flags, counters and sampling itself. An export discrepancy need not mean active protocol state changed. Match observation to the claim: stopping may change the behavior; neither shutdown sampling, locks, public APIs, dual reads nor race detection are universally required. Challenge specific unreliable reads, not all concurrent checks. Keep unresolved contracts, counterevidence, input legality and observation differences explicit; CheckRun owns execution status. An implementation/requirement discrepancy is the subject, not a conflict between requirement sources. Real contradictions remain conflicts.\n\nCONFIRMATION Reconstruct decisive relationships from the fixed test, actual constructors/producers and raw events; the plan's legality account is a claim to verify. Check prepared state, substituted calls and identity/context/generation across stages; constructible inputs or isolated fragments do not establish one legal history. Preserve relevant queues, callbacks, lock ownership and caller/transport duties. For waiting, missing replies or retained resources, trace waiter, result/cancel/close producer, normal shutdown entry and the observation's shutdown phase. Verify which owner/caller actually performs cleanup: no local timeout does not prove permanent waiting, and an available Close method does not prove it ran. A direct post-stop handler call differs from production dispatch still reaching it. Sourced local interface or exit duties need no whole-deployment proof. Review oracle, parsing, reached premises and completion together. Use rationale, source_ids, counterevidence, challenged_components and exact ReviewIssues for discrepancies; choose driver repair, encoding or F2/F3 by what changes, never weaken the written responsibility to rescue confirmation. Incompatible inputs are attribution gaps. Local functions, injectable storage, bounded initialization and substitute schedules remain valid when the sourced proposition permits them. Preserve measurements while correspondence is pending; complete local counterexamples survive independent wider-history or endpoint limits. New source counterevidence may challenge prior confirmation; an unobserved wider endpoint remains a limit.\nNECESSITY For S implies E, compare S when independently established E is false, or use equivalent supported implication encoding; never strengthen to S equals E or filter the result through applicability. In a complete implication comparison, observed S=false retains holds but supports only that S did not occur here, not E or universal consistency; S=true actually tests E. Missing results, identity or prerequisites are not observed falsity and cannot supply holds. Do not require every conditional branch to execute before confirming a complete local counterexample, or infer eventual success from a permitted pending control.\nPLAN {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"Concrete investigation of an accepted requirement; execution determines the observed result.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"description\": {\n      \"description\": \"This check\\u2019s discriminator, prefix, controls and observations; reference the accepted claim rather than restating it\",\n      \"title\": \"Description\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"claim_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Claim Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"binding_ids\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Binding Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"harness\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Harness\"\n    },\n    \"monitors\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EventMonitor\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Monitors\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"observable_properties\": {\n      \"description\": \"Direct route supports event_assertion and event_implication. Correlate prerequisite fields by alias; observe prerequisites and results from the same legal history. Unsupported general temporal properties must remain an explicit limitation.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ObservableProperty\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Observable Properties\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"uncertainties\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Uncertainties\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"description\",\n    \"claim_id\",\n    \"binding_ids\",\n    \"harness\",\n    \"monitors\",\n    \"observable_properties\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"DirectCheckPlan\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nDEFS ['Comparison', 'EventMonitor', 'EventRequirement', 'Grounding', 'Harness', 'ObservableProperty']\nCheckSubmission {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"sources\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Sources\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"feedback\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"repair_of\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Rejected operation ID whose complete draft this submission repairs\",\n      \"title\": \"Repair Of\"\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"check\",\n        \"revise_check\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Action\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"unit_id\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Unit Id\"\n    },\n    \"candidate\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CandidateSubmission\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"plan_path\": {\n      \"title\": \"Plan Path\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"harness_path\": {\n      \"title\": \"Harness Path\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"files\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Destination path to draft source path for helpers\",\n      \"title\": \"Files\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"previous_check_id\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Previous Check Id\"\n    },\n    \"repair_issue_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Exact issues whose driver premises the new harness legality answers; admission does not resolve them\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Repair Issue Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"encoding_revision\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EncodingRevision\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"rationale\",\n    \"action\",\n    \"plan_path\",\n    \"harness_path\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"CheckSubmission\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nClaimDraft {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"description\": \"A sourced requirement under explicit conditions, not the script for one experiment.\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"kind\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"obligation\",\n        \"assumption\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Kind\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"concern\": {\n      \"default\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"consensus_safety\",\n        \"bounded_liveness\",\n        \"implementation_semantics\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Concern\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"description\": \"Required relation across applicable objects and contexts; keep test instance IDs and timings in the check unless they determine applicability\",\n      \"title\": \"Description\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Located materials; file kinds do not establish normative authority\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"scope\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Scope\"\n    },\n    \"pending\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Pending\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"grounding\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Grounding\",\n      \"default\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [],\n        \"binding_ids\": [],\n        \"derivation\": \"\",\n        \"applicability\": \"\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": []\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"id\",\n    \"kind\",\n    \"description\",\n    \"source_ids\",\n    \"scope\",\n    \"pending\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ClaimDraft\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nBindingDraft {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"associations\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/BindingAssociation\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Associations\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"anchor\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CodeAnchor\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"material_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Material Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"symbol\": {\n      \"description\": \"Source symbol tied to a verified declaration, interface member or explicitly declared call-site anchor. The behavior range may be a narrow internal snippet. Do not substitute arbitrary words from the excerpt.\",\n      \"title\": \"Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"start_line\": {\n      \"title\": \"Start Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"end_line\": {\n      \"title\": \"End Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"title\": \"Description\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"pending\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Pending\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"associations\",\n    \"id\",\n    \"material_id\",\n    \"symbol\",\n    \"start_line\",\n    \"end_line\",\n    \"description\",\n    \"pending\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"BindingDraft\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The in-memory transport delivers heartbeats through the normal RPC queue, so it offers a test path without the concurrent heartbeat fast path. The timer settings are server-local, and the captured configuration contract does not require equal values across peers.\n\nI’ll ground the check in the `VerifyLeader` contract: after a higher-term leader has committed a command, a later verification on the isolated former leader must not report success. The test will observe both the competing commitment and the verification result, rather than infer failure from a missing quorum alone.\n"}}
