{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']\nfor k in ['BindingAssociation','CodeAnchor','Grounding']:\n print(k,json.dumps(s[k],indent=2))\nPY\nnl -ba ../agent-source/docs/README.md | sed -n '60,110p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/config.go | sed -n '270,316p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/api.go | sed -n '1008,1030p'\"","aggregated_output":"BindingAssociation {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"claim_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Claim Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"claim_id\",\n    \"source_ids\",\n    \"rationale\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"BindingAssociation\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nCodeAnchor {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"boundary_complete\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Boundary Complete\"\n    },\n    \"kind\": {\n      \"default\": \"declaration\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"declaration\",\n        \"interface_member\",\n        \"callsite\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Kind\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"material_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Material Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"start_line\": {\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Start Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"end_line\": {\n      \"minimum\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"End Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"symbol\": {\n      \"title\": \"Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"material_id\",\n    \"start_line\",\n    \"end_line\",\n    \"symbol\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"CodeAnchor\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nGrounding {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired implementation source materials; not Behavior or Binding IDs\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"expectation_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired materials supporting the expectation; not invented expectation labels. Explain normative applicability in derivation.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Expectation Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"binding_ids\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Binding Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"derivation\": {\n      \"default\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"This component\\u2019s sourced reasoning; cite accepted IDs instead of repeating their full argument\",\n      \"title\": \"Derivation\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"applicability\": {\n      \"default\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"Conditions for this component, including any added assumptions or omitted protections\",\n      \"title\": \"Applicability\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"unresolved\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Unresolved\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"conflicts\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Conflicts\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"alternatives\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Alternatives\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"title\": \"Grounding\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n    60\t* AppliedIndex - get the index of the last log entry applied to the FSM\n    61\t* GetConfiguration - return the latest cluster configuration\n    62\t* LastContact - get the last time this peer made contact with the leader\n    63\t* LastIndex - get the index of the latest stored log entry\n    64\t* Leader - get the address of the peer that is currently the leader\n    65\t* Snapshot - snapshot the current state of the FSM into a file\n    66\t* State - return the state of the peer\n    67\t* Stats - return some stats about the peer and the cluster\n    68\t\n    69\t## Threads\n    70\t\n    71\tRaft uses the following threads to handle operations. The name of the thread is in bold,\n    72\tand a short description of the operation handled by the thread follows. The main thread is\n    73\tresponsible for handling many operations.\n    74\t\n    75\t* **run** (main thread) - different behaviour based on peer state\n    76\t   * follower\n    77\t      * processRPC (from rpcCh)\n    78\t         * AppendEntries\n    79\t         * RequestVote\n    80\t         * InstallSnapshot\n    81\t         * TimeoutNow\n    82\t      * liveBootstrap (from bootstrapCh)\n    83\t      * periodic heartbeatTimer (HeartbeatTimeout)\n    84\t   * candidate - starts an election for itself when called\n    85\t      * processRPC (from rpcCh) - same as follower\n    86\t      * acceptVote (from askPeerForVote)\n    87\t   * leader - first starts replication to all peers, and applies a Noop log to ensure the new leader has committed up to the commit index\n    88\t      * processRPC (from rpcCh) - same as follower, however we don’t actually expect to receive any RPCs other than a RequestVote\n    89\t      * leadershipTransfer (from leadershipTransferCh) - \n    90\t      * commit (from commitCh) -\n    91\t      * verifyLeader (from verifyCh) -\n    92\t      * user restore snapshot (from userRestoreCh) -\n    93\t      * changeConfig (from configurationChangeCh) -\n    94\t      * dispatchLogs (from applyCh) - handle client Raft.Apply requests by persisting logs to disk, and notifying replication goroutines to replicate the new logs\n    95\t      * checkLease (periodically LeaseTimeout) -\n    96\t* **runFSM** - has exclusive access to the FSM, all reads and writes must send a message to this thread. Commands:\n    97\t   * apply logs to the FSM, from the fsmMutateCh, from processLogs, from leaderLoop (leader) or appendEntries RPC (follower/candidate)\n    98\t   * restore a snapshot to the FSM, from the fsmMutateCh, from restoreUserSnapshot (leader) or installSnapshot RPC (follower/candidate)\n    99\t   * capture snapshot, from fsmSnapshotCh, from takeSnapshot (runSnapshot thread)\n   100\t* **runSnapshot** - handles the slower part of taking a snapshot. From a pointer captured by the FSM.Snapshot operation, this thread persists the snapshot by calling FSMSnapshot.Persist. Also calls compactLogs to delete old logs.\n   101\t   * periodically (SnapshotInterval) takeSnapshot for log compaction\n   102\t   * user snapshot, from userSnapshotCh, takeSnapshot to return to the user\n   103\t* **askPeerForVote (candidate only)** - short lived goroutine that synchronously sends a RequestVote RPC to all voting peers, and waits for the response. One goroutine per voting peer.\n   104\t* **replicate (leader only)** - long running goroutine that synchronously sends log entry AppendEntry RPCs to all peers. Also starts the heartbeat thread, and possibly the pipelineDecode thread. Runs sendLatestSnapshot when AppendEntry fails.\n   105\t   * **heartbeat (leader only)** - long running goroutine that synchronously sends heartbeat AppendEntry RPCs to all peers.\n   106\t   * **pipelineDecode (leader only)**\n   270\t\t// send an entire snapshot. The value passed here updates the setting at runtime\n   271\t\t// which will take effect as soon as the next snapshot completes and truncation\n   272\t\t// occurs.\n   273\t\tTrailingLogs uint64\n   274\t\n   275\t\t// SnapshotInterval controls how often we check if we should perform a snapshot.\n   276\t\t// We randomly stagger between this value and 2x this value to avoid the entire\n   277\t\t// cluster from performing a snapshot at once.\n   278\t\tSnapshotInterval time.Duration\n   279\t\n   280\t\t// SnapshotThreshold controls how many outstanding logs there must be before\n   281\t\t// we perform a snapshot. This is to prevent excessive snapshots when we can\n   282\t\t// just replay a small set of logs.\n   283\t\tSnapshotThreshold uint64\n   284\t\n   285\t\t// HeartbeatTimeout specifies the time in follower state without\n   286\t\t// a leader before we attempt an election.\n   287\t\tHeartbeatTimeout time.Duration\n   288\t\n   289\t\t// ElectionTimeout specifies the time in candidate state without\n   290\t\t// a leader before we attempt an election.\n   291\t\tElectionTimeout time.Duration\n   292\t}\n   293\t\n   294\t// apply sets the reloadable fields on the passed Config to the values in\n   295\t// `ReloadableConfig`. It returns a copy of Config with the fields from this\n   296\t// ReloadableConfig set.\n   297\tfunc (rc *ReloadableConfig) apply(to Config) Config {\n   298\t\tto.TrailingLogs = rc.TrailingLogs\n   299\t\tto.SnapshotInterval = rc.SnapshotInterval\n   300\t\tto.SnapshotThreshold = rc.SnapshotThreshold\n   301\t\tto.HeartbeatTimeout = rc.HeartbeatTimeout\n   302\t\tto.ElectionTimeout = rc.ElectionTimeout\n   303\t\treturn to\n   304\t}\n   305\t\n   306\t// fromConfig copies the reloadable fields from the passed Config.\n   307\tfunc (rc *ReloadableConfig) fromConfig(from Config) {\n   308\t\trc.TrailingLogs = from.TrailingLogs\n   309\t\trc.SnapshotInterval = from.SnapshotInterval\n   310\t\trc.SnapshotThreshold = from.SnapshotThreshold\n   311\t\trc.HeartbeatTimeout = from.HeartbeatTimeout\n   312\t\trc.ElectionTimeout = from.ElectionTimeout\n   313\t}\n   314\t\n   315\t// DefaultConfig returns a Config with usable defaults.\n   316\tfunc DefaultConfig() *Config {\n  1008\t\n  1009\t// Shutdown is used to stop the Raft background routines.\n  1010\t// This is not a graceful operation. Provides a future that\n  1011\t// can be used to block until all background routines have exited.\n  1012\tfunc (r *Raft) Shutdown() Future {\n  1013\t\tr.shutdownLock.Lock()\n  1014\t\tdefer r.shutdownLock.Unlock()\n  1015\t\n  1016\t\tif !r.shutdown {\n  1017\t\t\tclose(r.shutdownCh)\n  1018\t\t\tr.shutdown = true\n  1019\t\t\tr.setState(Shutdown)\n  1020\t\t\treturn &shutdownFuture{r}\n  1021\t\t}\n  1022\t\n  1023\t\t// avoid closing transport twice\n  1024\t\treturn &shutdownFuture{nil}\n  1025\t}\n  1026\t\n  1027\t// Snapshot is used to manually force Raft to take a snapshot. Returns a future\n  1028\t// that can be used to block until complete, and that contains a function that\n  1029\t// can be used to open the snapshot.\n  1030\tfunc (r *Raft) Snapshot() SnapshotFuture {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'))\nc=r['candidates'][0]\nq=c['question'].copy()\nnew=[('S-inmem-routing','inmem_transport.go',38,243,'code_observation'),('S-timer-contract','config.go',137,205,'interface_statement'),('S-config-validation','config.go',315,376,'code_observation'),('S-membership-api','api.go',939,976,'interface_statement'),('S-shutdown-api','api.go',1009,1025,'interface_statement')]\nsources=[dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k) for i,f,a,b,k in new]\nq['source_ids']=sorted(set(q['source_ids']+[x[0] for x in new]))\nq['unknowns']=['A production execution must establish the stable mixed configuration, a higher-term leader and its committed command before verification admission, then observe the same VerifyLeader future result.','The controlled schedule must account for pre-partition in-flight replies before attributing false confirmation specifically to nonvoters.']\nq['disposition']='ready_for_check'\nq['trigger_rationale']='Source tracing confirms that nonvoter peers register verify futures and positive heartbeat/append notifications reach the same identity-free tally. InmemTransport delivers real RPCs through the role loop, and separately configurable per-server election/lease timers provide a legal interval for competing leadership to precede the old leader lease check. A full live prefix distinguishes a false exposed authority result from a merely suspect local tally. The follower commit-bound question remains a separate unresolved producer-history question.'\nclaim=dict(id='C-verify-current-authority',kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='In a fixed cluster configuration, a VerifyLeader invocation on a former leader must not return success when, before that invocation, a different voter quorum has elected a higher-term leader and that leader has committed a command, while the former leader remains isolated from that quorum. Responses from nonvoters cannot make the former leader current again.',source_ids=['S-client','S-config','S-membership-api','S-vote','S-election','S-timer-contract'],scope=dict(description='Live non-Byzantine Raft peers using a stable mixed voter/nonvoter configuration, valid server-local timer configurations and a network partition. The higher-term election and completed command precede the VerifyLeader invocation. No membership mutation, manual restore or storage failure overlaps that interval.',assumptions=['Transport returns only actual peer responses or delivery errors; no forged replies.','A majority of configured voters establishes the competing leader and its new command.','Each server satisfies Config validation; timer values may differ across servers, as the captured Config API specifies per-server settings and no cross-server equality rule.'],excluded=['Claiming that any missing response is a deadline violation.','Guaranteeing that the current leader FSM has applied every committed entry without a caller barrier.','Arbitrary direct handler calls or invented preloaded election history.','Byzantine peers, reused server identities, and caller-forced history replacement.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S-verify','S-verify-vote','S-loop','S-lease','S-repl-start','S-heartbeat','S-inmem-routing','S-config-validation'],expectation_ids=['S-client','S-config','S-membership-api','S-timer-contract'],binding_ids=['BD-verify-register','BD-verify-result','BD-verify-api'],derivation='S-client states that VerifyLeader ensures the peer is still leader and may prevent stale FSM reads after leadership loss. This obligation asks only for rejection of an independently established obsolete authority, not freshness of a current leader FSM. S-config and S-membership-api distinguish voter from nonvoter participation. The implementation contrast is voter-count quorumSize versus all-replicator registration; S-loop consumes the tally without a second voter qualification. S-lease independently ends local authority but is timer-scheduled, not a prerequisite of VerifyLeader success. S-timer-contract describes server-local timers; S-config-validation enforces each local lease <= heartbeat <= election setting, with no requirement that values match across peers.',applicability='The check must witness the higher term and completed command before invocation and keep the partition in place until the result. A valid local timer configuration alone is not proof that the desired history was reached.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['The old peer may process its voter-only lease check or a negative reply before completion and correctly return an error.','Old in-flight voter replies could explain a result unless their lifecycle is accounted for; this must remain visible in the harness and correspondence review.']))\ndef bind(id,mat,sym,a,b,desc):\n return dict(id=id,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=[mat,'S-client'],rationale=desc)])\nbindings=[bind('BD-verify-register','S-verify','verifyLeader',965,988,'Initializes voter-based threshold but registers all replication peers for the authority check.'),bind('BD-verify-result','S-loop','leaderLoop',844,868,'Consumes the verification tally and exposes nil completion when it reaches quorumSize.'),bind('BD-verify-api','S-client','VerifyLeader',880,895,'Public authority-check contract and invocation path returning the verification future.')]\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=[c['id'],'S-inmem-routing','S-timer-contract','S-config-validation','S-membership-api','B-verify-register','B-verify-support','B-verify-consume','F-verify-tally'],answered='Positive notification paths do not re-check peer suffrage: verifyLeader registers every replication peer, notifyAll drains that peer map, and vote(true) increments the shared counter. InmemTransport does not use a concurrent heartbeat fast path and permits normal network disconnection. Config documents server-local heartbeat/election/lease settings, validates their local ordering, and does not supply a cross-server equality requirement. Therefore a sourced full-history check can distinguish stale authority success before the old peer lease check from an internal tally anomaly.',remaining=q['unknowns'],understanding='updated',rationale='This source work fixes the applicable current-authority obligation while retaining lease protection and reply-lifecycle attribution as execution premises. No target execution or defect verdict is claimed.')\nsub=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,sources=sources,feedback=feedback,rationale='Ground the authority-confirmation responsibility in the public VerifyLeader contract, using actual server-local configuration and routing mechanisms; construct the live partition witness next.')\njson.dump(sub,open('obligation-submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 make_obligation.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json')); p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['obligation-submission.json'],text=True,capture_output=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
